WEBVTT

00:13.854 --> 00:17.941
We have to part ways today, Young Master.

00:19.109 --> 00:20.694
Will I ever see you again?

00:24.281 --> 00:26.450
When this child goes to elementary school

00:26.533 --> 00:30.871
and if the Yatsuka family is willing
to hire me back despite my weakened state,

00:30.954 --> 00:32.956
then we can meet again.

00:33.832 --> 00:37.753
But you'll be big and strong by then.

00:40.172 --> 00:43.091
Be careful in the dark.

00:55.312 --> 00:56.605
That hurt…

00:56.688 --> 00:59.733
Oh, drat. That's not good.

01:05.405 --> 01:07.449
Yep, looks like we're stuck.

01:08.033 --> 01:11.912
Rest assured,
I've already called for backup.

01:11.995 --> 01:12.913
But the thing is…

01:13.413 --> 01:15.123
it's going to take four hours.

01:15.207 --> 01:16.541
Four hours?!

01:40.315 --> 01:42.567
Nice one! Bingo!

01:42.651 --> 01:45.362
Wait, how many points was that?

01:45.445 --> 01:50.742
Don't ask me. It's your job
to keep track of your score.

01:52.744 --> 01:55.705
So close. Dang, just missed it…

01:55.789 --> 01:58.208
You're trying too hard, Toshiro.

01:58.291 --> 02:00.418
The windows aren't there
for target practice.

02:00.502 --> 02:02.504
Oh, Young Master.

02:02.587 --> 02:05.632
We kept our distance
to avoid waking you up,

02:05.715 --> 02:08.093
but I guess you heard us from the bus.

02:08.176 --> 02:11.096
While you're here,
wanna play some Ultimate Bingo?

02:11.179 --> 02:12.639
It's okay, I'll pass.

02:14.266 --> 02:15.976
Hey Kanaeno,

02:16.059 --> 02:19.146
why do you call Akira "Young Master"?

02:22.190 --> 02:26.778
I worked for the Yatsuka family
when Young Master was a tiny boy.

02:26.862 --> 02:29.906
He was scared to pee by himself,

02:29.990 --> 02:34.661
so I held his hand
and escorted him to the toilet.

02:34.744 --> 02:35.579
Hey!

02:35.662 --> 02:38.665
Wow, awesome. That's another bingo.

02:49.009 --> 02:51.970
Crap, crap, crap! How'd that happen?!

02:52.053 --> 02:53.972
Run, run, run!

03:06.067 --> 03:08.486
Dr. Kudai and Ken Hikasa?

03:08.570 --> 03:10.989
If we're trusting Toshiro's ability,

03:11.072 --> 03:16.912
then Ivy… or rather, Mukuru Izumi's
transfloration was the opposition's ploy.

03:16.995 --> 03:18.246
I see…

03:18.330 --> 03:24.127
There's public outcry, angry protests,
and rioting at the Transfloration Board.

03:24.711 --> 03:26.588
Before long, we'll have casualties.

03:27.339 --> 03:31.760
I heard the higher-ups are thinking about
downsizing Transflora Medical No. 4, too.

03:32.344 --> 03:37.265
We have to uncover the truth ASAP
and debunk the opposition's false claims.

03:37.933 --> 03:39.434
Otherwise, we're done for.

03:43.313 --> 03:44.773
For us to win,

03:44.856 --> 03:49.527
we'll need solid proof that Dr. Kudai
and Hikasa from the opposition

03:49.611 --> 03:51.947
are responsible for creating Ivy, right?

03:52.030 --> 03:55.075
If we get Ivy's seedling reports
from the doctor himself…

03:55.158 --> 03:59.204
To get our hands on that,
we'd need to locate Dr. Kudai first.

03:59.287 --> 04:01.164
He's been MIA for over 40 years!

04:01.748 --> 04:03.917
Okay, so what's the plan?

04:04.000 --> 04:08.171
How about we
capture Ken Hikasa for questioning?

04:08.255 --> 04:12.467
I can serve as a lie detector
and sniff out the truth right away.

04:12.550 --> 04:16.930
Hikasa's got private bodyguards.
Well, more like his army.

04:17.013 --> 04:20.308
He's got five or six of them
guarding his ass.

04:20.809 --> 04:24.396
Can anybody else
at Transflora Medical help us?

04:24.479 --> 04:27.691
And the police. Akira's aunt, maybe?

04:27.774 --> 04:31.778
Before that, we need evidence
to place suspicion on the opposition.

04:31.861 --> 04:35.156
Without any evidence,
nobody's going to help us.

04:35.865 --> 04:39.160
Okay, so the five of us
need to work this out ourselves.

04:42.956 --> 04:46.418
In that case, I'll check out the Archives.

04:46.501 --> 04:47.419
The Archives?

04:47.919 --> 04:50.588
What are the Archives?

04:51.256 --> 04:56.553
<i>A secret safe at the Transfloration Board,</i>
<i>Transflora Medical's parent organization.</i>

04:56.636 --> 05:00.098
<i>Transfloration's theoretical framework</i>
<i>and early research records</i>

05:00.181 --> 05:05.020
<i>are hidden there to prevent</i>
<i>outside reproduction and ethical collapse.</i>

05:05.103 --> 05:08.315
The transfloration policy's black box,
so to speak.

05:08.398 --> 05:12.444
You're right. We might find a lead
on Kudai's whereabouts there.

05:13.028 --> 05:15.947
I'll check domestic universities
and private enterprises

05:16.031 --> 05:19.409
to find the lab where the doctor
may have created Ivy's seed.

05:19.492 --> 05:20.327
Okay.

05:20.410 --> 05:24.080
I'll snoop around Transflora Medical
and see what I can find.

05:24.164 --> 05:29.210
If we find a clue leading to the doctor,
we can pull this off.

05:32.130 --> 05:33.423
Let's win this.

05:41.264 --> 05:43.349
<i>Kudai… Kudai…</i>

05:44.476 --> 05:45.435
<i>Kudai…</i>

05:51.066 --> 05:54.444
Looks like we can't go home today…

05:58.948 --> 06:01.910
No, I haven't found a thing here.

06:02.452 --> 06:04.204
How were the Archives?

06:05.789 --> 06:07.874
<i>They wouldn't listen to me.</i>

06:08.458 --> 06:11.336
<i>We'll just have to try</i>
<i>different approaches.</i>

06:26.226 --> 06:29.646
Please sign our petition
to abolish transfloration!

06:29.729 --> 06:32.148
Transflora Medical brings us all misery!

06:32.232 --> 06:34.651
How do you live with yourself?!

06:40.740 --> 06:43.827
What gives you the right
to sulk about this?

06:45.787 --> 06:49.290
<i>I won't forgive you.</i>

07:09.185 --> 07:11.855
HOSPITAL

07:29.038 --> 07:30.123
How much is it worth?

07:30.707 --> 07:34.002
Antibiotics and fever medicine.
Some have been taken, though.

07:35.044 --> 07:37.672
Wouldn't it be better to keep those?

07:38.465 --> 07:42.093
People collapse every day
at your workplace, right?

07:42.760 --> 07:47.265
I urgently need the money.
I want to get out of here fast.

07:52.103 --> 07:54.272
<i>Do Spiriflora really need this much care?</i>

07:54.856 --> 07:57.775
For Spiriflora with claimants in the city,

07:57.859 --> 08:01.779
we sever the remaining skulls or spines
to make them look nice before delivery.

08:02.780 --> 08:09.537
<i>Their family and friends wouldn't want</i>
<i>those human parts still attached.</i>

08:09.621 --> 08:14.792
Once you're fully bloomed, you can return
to the city with a one-way shipping fee.

08:15.376 --> 08:18.046
We want to go back
while we're still alive.

08:18.713 --> 08:21.966
Then you need to bribe
a high-ranking government official

08:22.050 --> 08:24.219
to repair your credit score.

08:24.802 --> 08:25.803
How much will it cost?

08:26.888 --> 08:29.349
Per person, it's three million yen.

08:35.063 --> 08:37.649
We only earn 500 yen a day…

08:38.858 --> 08:40.276
So there's no way of going back…

08:42.445 --> 08:43.947
This is ridiculous.

08:53.289 --> 08:54.541
<i>I wake up at 8:00 a.m.</i>

08:55.291 --> 08:56.709
<i>From nine to twelve o'clock,</i>

08:56.793 --> 09:00.505
<i>I scrape off the blood and flesh</i>
<i>stuck to the beds and floors.</i>

09:01.589 --> 09:04.926
<i>For lunch, I drink soup</i>
<i>that tastes like salt water.</i>

09:05.468 --> 09:10.682
<i>From 1:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m., I trim off</i>
<i>the rotten limbs of these plant people.</i>

09:12.976 --> 09:14.769
<i>That earns me 500 yen a day.</i>

09:15.853 --> 09:19.983
<i>If I set aside 200 yen every day,</i>
<i>saving up three million yen would take…</i>

09:45.216 --> 09:46.301
Meg?

09:46.884 --> 09:47.719
Meg?

09:48.303 --> 09:49.262
Meg!

09:50.388 --> 09:51.806
Meg!

09:57.312 --> 09:58.855
Meg!

09:59.897 --> 10:02.775
Thank goodness.
I thought you'd been kidnapped.

10:03.276 --> 10:05.737
Don't wander by yourself.
It's dangerous here--

10:10.825 --> 10:11.951
Meg…

10:15.371 --> 10:16.497
Did you…

10:17.999 --> 10:20.460
What did you do?! Don't be stupid!

10:20.543 --> 10:21.377
I want out!

10:22.003 --> 10:24.213
I'm going back, no matter what!

10:25.381 --> 10:29.010
Dad, do you have any right
to complain about the money I earn?

10:29.093 --> 10:32.513
You're the one who ruined my life
in the first place!

10:33.473 --> 10:37.352
At this rate,
it'll take 40 years to get out of here.

10:37.435 --> 10:39.812
By then, I'll be 55 years old!

10:43.149 --> 10:46.653
Give me my life back…

10:53.534 --> 10:54.535
Transfloration?

10:55.536 --> 10:59.957
I'll bring back the subsidy
and leave Paupertown with my daughter.

11:00.875 --> 11:02.835
I've made up my mind.

11:03.753 --> 11:06.339
You probably won't succeed.

11:06.923 --> 11:10.718
Here, you're not allowed
to use the subsidy on yourself.

11:11.302 --> 11:15.723
"Not allowed"? What do you mean?
I'm the one doing the procedure!

11:15.807 --> 11:21.729
Transfloration subsidies in Paupertown
are split among the majority for survival.

11:22.313 --> 11:27.235
If the town's authorities catch you,
they'll confiscate the subsidy.

11:28.319 --> 11:32.240
<i>They're a group of barbarians</i>
<i>swinging metal pipes around.</i>

11:32.323 --> 11:36.869
You should've made this decision
while you were still in the city.

11:39.414 --> 11:42.333
I'm going regardless.

11:44.293 --> 11:47.255
I'm getting Meg's life back.

11:49.841 --> 11:51.509
I'll undergo transfloration.

11:52.093 --> 11:56.431
I'll bring back the subsidy
so that we can leave together.

12:08.609 --> 12:09.986
Thank you.

12:11.571 --> 12:14.157
Thanks, Dad.

12:15.950 --> 12:17.869
Thank you, Dad.

12:18.995 --> 12:20.580
Thank you…

12:23.291 --> 12:24.917
Hold onto this.

12:27.044 --> 12:28.421
A watch?

12:29.005 --> 12:32.008
It's a watch I got from my grandmother.

12:33.009 --> 12:35.094
It doesn't have many time markers…

12:35.970 --> 12:38.431
These were popular back in the day.

12:39.015 --> 12:41.851
When the hour hand makes
a full rotation, it's morning.

12:41.934 --> 12:43.936
One more rotation, and it's night again.

12:44.729 --> 12:45.897
Morning…

12:46.522 --> 12:50.735
If I don't come back,
you can sell this for a little money.

12:59.285 --> 13:03.706
I'll be right back.
Until then, you have to be strong…

13:06.292 --> 13:09.212
<i>I can go home. I can get out of here!</i>

13:09.795 --> 13:11.756
<i>Back to warmth and light.</i>

13:12.298 --> 13:16.469
<i>I can reunite with my friends,</i>
<i>my teachers, and Saito, too!</i>

13:17.553 --> 13:18.971
<i>Scrambled eggs with ketchup.</i>

13:19.055 --> 13:20.973
<i>I can eat consommé soup, too!</i>

13:22.058 --> 13:26.354
<i>Shopping malls,</i>
<i>clean water, and a soft bed…</i>

13:27.855 --> 13:29.815
<i>Everything will go back to normal.</i>

13:31.776 --> 13:34.946
Wait… Please…

13:35.738 --> 13:37.990
Don't cut off my right hand…

13:38.491 --> 13:43.371
I still… want to draw… please…

13:46.165 --> 13:48.000
It's rotten, so I'm chopping it off.

13:56.968 --> 14:00.263
It's already been two weeks, hasn't it?

14:00.846 --> 14:04.225
Your daddy got caught.

14:05.476 --> 14:07.895
Now you're trapped here forever.

14:16.112 --> 14:17.280
Congrats.

14:25.746 --> 14:29.667
How dare you! Don't make fun of me!

14:35.089 --> 14:37.300
Hey! Stop it!

14:37.383 --> 14:39.427
What have you done?!

14:42.013 --> 14:43.014
You're fired!

14:48.352 --> 14:50.021
Still alive?

14:51.022 --> 14:52.231
Take her away.

14:55.484 --> 14:59.447
<i>Transflora Medical, Transflora Medical</i>

15:00.031 --> 15:04.452
<i>In your final days of life,</i>
<i>why not do something to benefit others?</i>

15:04.535 --> 15:08.122
<i>Transflora Medical, Transflora Medical</i>

15:08.205 --> 15:09.457
<i>Why…</i>

15:10.541 --> 15:12.460
<i>I told him, "Thank you."</i>

15:13.544 --> 15:15.129
<i>How could I be so cruel?</i>

15:17.673 --> 15:21.594
<i>Life doesn't end. Life continues on.</i>

15:21.677 --> 15:26.599
<i>A subsidy of ten million yen</i>
<i>for the sake of Earth and everyone else.</i>

15:26.682 --> 15:29.644
<i>Why not become a vessel for our flowers?</i>

15:33.814 --> 15:39.111
<i>In your final days of life,</i>
<i>why not do something to benefit others?</i>

15:41.822 --> 15:44.617
Yeah… Yeah.

15:46.661 --> 15:49.372
I have zero leads.

15:49.455 --> 15:53.167
We haven't found
any definite proof either.

15:53.668 --> 15:57.922
But we found someone close to the doctor,
so we're heading there now.

15:58.464 --> 16:00.508
All right, bye.

16:02.969 --> 16:07.390
I found out from some archived materials
at the Transfloration History Museum

16:07.473 --> 16:09.892
that Kudai has a younger brother.

16:09.976 --> 16:11.477
You really did your research.

16:11.978 --> 16:14.021
Well, I did what I could.

16:14.105 --> 16:17.149
<i>In other news,</i>
<i>a major press conference will be held</i>

16:17.233 --> 16:22.905
<i>by the anti-transfloration movement's</i>
<i>new "Glory Days Party" in five days.</i>

16:23.906 --> 16:26.909
<i>Sparked by recent crimes</i>
<i>committed by a transfloration patient,</i>

16:26.993 --> 16:30.246
<i>protests have continued</i>
<i>in front of the Transfloration Board.</i>

16:31.247 --> 16:37.003
<i>This upcoming speech is making big waves</i>
<i>as societal views continue to shift.</i>

16:44.051 --> 16:47.930
Glory Days Party? How pointless is that?

16:48.514 --> 16:50.433
Nothing's gonna change anyway.

16:51.017 --> 16:53.853
I'm attending the speech.
I'm protesting, too.

16:54.520 --> 16:55.938
Seriously, Saito?

16:56.022 --> 16:58.858
If it weren't for transfloration, Meg…

16:58.941 --> 17:01.193
I mean, Okumura could've lived normally.

17:02.236 --> 17:05.072
We're better off without transfloration.

17:37.021 --> 17:38.439
STOP TRANSFLORATION!

17:38.522 --> 17:40.941
THE TRANSFLORATION BOARD
IS THE ROOT OF ALL EVIL!

17:51.035 --> 17:52.787
MR. KUDAI

17:52.870 --> 17:54.705
You're Mitsuru Kudai, right?

17:55.206 --> 17:57.708
I'm Horai from Transflora Medical No. 4.

17:58.459 --> 18:00.461
I'm Kamiya. I work there too.

18:05.049 --> 18:07.176
I'll cut right to the chase.

18:08.511 --> 18:13.766
If you happen to know where
your older brother, Dr. Otaro Kudai is,

18:14.433 --> 18:15.851
could you tell us his whereabouts?

18:22.108 --> 18:23.901
<i>Hatred and fear.</i>

18:24.610 --> 18:26.028
Leave.

18:26.612 --> 18:29.490
Could you at least
answer with "yes" or "no"?

18:29.990 --> 18:30.825
Leave.

18:30.908 --> 18:32.201
I'm not leaving!

18:32.284 --> 18:36.247
Listen here, Mitsuru.
We're trying to throw the doctor in jail.

18:36.330 --> 18:40.000
Wha… Idiot! Why would you say that?

18:40.084 --> 18:41.210
Oh.

18:43.129 --> 18:45.548
Why didn't you say so?

18:46.257 --> 18:48.300
I hate my brother.

18:48.801 --> 18:51.428
If you want him behind bars, be my guest.

18:52.680 --> 18:55.391
But I honestly don't know where he is.

18:56.142 --> 19:00.146
There's no way to contact him, either.

19:02.231 --> 19:03.816
<i>He's not lying.</i>

19:05.860 --> 19:08.445
Why do you hate your brother?

19:09.071 --> 19:10.531
When we were kids,

19:10.614 --> 19:17.037
he cut off two of my fingers in my sleep
just to compare them to an anatomy book.

19:17.663 --> 19:20.875
He doesn't understand people's pain.

19:21.792 --> 19:26.839
Even as a scientist, he was obsessed
with demonstrating his own research.

19:26.922 --> 19:30.968
That man never once
showed consideration toward others.

19:31.552 --> 19:34.096
On the other hand, losing my fingers

19:34.180 --> 19:36.974
made me more sensitive
to other people's pain.

19:37.683 --> 19:41.312
<i>Lately, the joints of my fingers</i>
<i>have been aching constantly,</i>

19:41.896 --> 19:45.816
<i>echoing the cries of those</i>
<i>suffering because of transfloration.</i>

19:45.900 --> 19:50.321
You people working in transfloration
are the same as my brother.

19:50.905 --> 19:52.823
You can't hear these cries.

19:55.159 --> 19:57.119
That's not true.

19:57.203 --> 19:58.454
Really?

19:59.038 --> 20:01.457
Then why do you still work for them?

20:05.044 --> 20:08.297
My vote is going to the Glory Days Party.

20:10.716 --> 20:12.968
Hey, I'm still suspended…

20:13.052 --> 20:13.969
Just come.

20:14.053 --> 20:16.222
What is it? Seriously…

20:21.852 --> 20:24.230
Can you hear this Spiriflor?

20:28.359 --> 20:29.777
Does it hate me?

20:31.487 --> 20:32.780
I don't hear anything.

20:33.572 --> 20:37.660
But it knows that you're really nervous.

20:38.160 --> 20:39.620
I see…

20:46.001 --> 20:48.170
Did you hear it say something?

20:49.672 --> 20:51.632
It said, "I won't forgive you."

21:08.732 --> 21:12.111
I saw tons of awful stuff in Paupertown.

21:13.195 --> 21:16.031
The whole place was steeped
in misery and madness,

21:16.115 --> 21:18.909
like blood was seeping
from the buildings themselves.

21:20.119 --> 21:26.166
According to Akira, that horrifying sight
is the same as the transfloration policy.

21:26.250 --> 21:28.669
Sacrificing a few to save the many.

21:30.921 --> 21:35.092
But in my case,
I'm not working for a greater cause.

21:36.135 --> 21:38.804
I'm just desperately trying
to hold on to what I have.

21:41.390 --> 21:46.395
Even though I know people are miserable,
I can't get off this train.

21:49.648 --> 21:52.234
Yomiko, do you feel a greater cause here?

21:54.403 --> 21:58.324
I was on the same train,
acting oblivious the whole time.

21:58.991 --> 22:01.410
I'm just working to make a living.

22:02.870 --> 22:08.959
All that stuff about someone having
to provide oxygen to save the planet

22:09.668 --> 22:11.837
or to secure a future
for the next generation…

22:12.921 --> 22:15.883
I just memorized all that
for the job interview.

22:20.596 --> 22:22.473
Should I get off the train?

22:27.811 --> 22:29.772
Don't you dare get off.

22:47.915 --> 22:52.961
<i>Toshiro knows what would happen</i>
<i>if he got off this train.</i>

22:54.254 --> 22:56.340
<i>We'd lose our seat.</i>

23:21.240 --> 23:24.993
<i>I won't let Toshiro be miserable again.</i>

23:31.166 --> 23:33.418
<i>I'll protect him, no matter what.</i>

25:15.604 --> 25:20.609
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
